[{:db/id 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-481bd08b-bf47-54b5-b36c-cbccf6d7d5b3" "question-9bc932a7-b704-59fd-b0c1-c79e29ca1ef0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4087990a-4ed6-57e2-a3df-7711bffc8cc9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cbafb4bb-6bd6-540c-9367-06ab0b677b70" "question-a285feed-066b-52a2-a5c2-8c1c741cc3d0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-481bd08b-bf47-54b5-b36c-cbccf6d7d5b3" :question/id #uuid "481bd08b-bf47-54b5-b36c-cbccf6d7d5b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-210757" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-064b270e-fcf7-5b15-ad01-0cc140059469"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-064b270e-fcf7-5b15-ad01-0cc140059469" :answer-field/id #uuid "064b270e-fcf7-5b15-ad01-0cc140059469" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b4d86307-444b-5404-bf96-e83b782452e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4d86307-444b-5404-bf96-e83b782452e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4d86307-444b-5404-bf96-e83b782452e7" :answer/id #uuid "b4d86307-444b-5404-bf96-e83b782452e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9bc932a7-b704-59fd-b0c1-c79e29ca1ef0" :question/id #uuid "9bc932a7-b704-59fd-b0c1-c79e29ca1ef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-126151" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-x/20},\\, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-t/20}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-t/20}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/20}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-x/20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ 1-{e}^{-x/20}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d1d5c23-5aca-5a94-9f2b-7f2199c25b68"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d1d5c23-5aca-5a94-9f2b-7f2199c25b68" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d1d5c23-5aca-5a94-9f2b-7f2199c25b68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ad1adf91-dd13-599a-aacf-34ab3e99b819" :answer-field/choices ["answer-63f468a1-66c1-59cb-86ef-0e77953938a7" "answer-713d0b3e-c9bb-554a-b337-a9f036666fa2" "answer-36a08189-b91b-5a20-b7ab-cd5b33daebf3" "answer-ad1adf91-dd13-599a-aacf-34ab3e99b819" "answer-74a5f07c-c3bf-5c2c-a586-05b1a17ea2f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63f468a1-66c1-59cb-86ef-0e77953938a7" :answer/id #uuid "63f468a1-66c1-59cb-86ef-0e77953938a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{{e}^{-x/20}}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-713d0b3e-c9bb-554a-b337-a9f036666fa2" :answer/id #uuid "713d0b3e-c9bb-554a-b337-a9f036666fa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-20{e}^{-x/20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36a08189-b91b-5a20-b7ab-cd5b33daebf3" :answer/id #uuid "36a08189-b91b-5a20-b7ab-cd5b33daebf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/20}}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad1adf91-dd13-599a-aacf-34ab3e99b819" :answer/id #uuid "ad1adf91-dd13-599a-aacf-34ab3e99b819" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{e}^{-x/20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74a5f07c-c3bf-5c2c-a586-05b1a17ea2f2" :answer/id #uuid "74a5f07c-c3bf-5c2c-a586-05b1a17ea2f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-x/20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186419955 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{108}x(x+2),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 6,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{108}t(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{324}{t}^{2}(t+3)|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186419941 :answer-field/correct "answer-b909905a-559d-5031-bfb7-8668badafec2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b909905a-559d-5031-bfb7-8668badafec2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b909905a-559d-5031-bfb7-8668badafec2" :answer/id #uuid "b909905a-559d-5031-bfb7-8668badafec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}(x+3)}{324}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4087990a-4ed6-57e2-a3df-7711bffc8cc9" :question/id #uuid "4087990a-4ed6-57e2-a3df-7711bffc8cc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-89659" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}(x-2),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<3 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $3\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ {\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{x}\\frac{2}{3}(t-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{3}t(t-4)|}_{3}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}x(x-4)+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4e5a55d3-f519-5435-8ffd-ee8305a73bcc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e5a55d3-f519-5435-8ffd-ee8305a73bcc" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e5a55d3-f519-5435-8ffd-ee8305a73bcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2ea5a4d8-cee6-5f5b-9559-0597059ae4e9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-624998d8-03eb-57ee-930b-8fdefbbf7c6a" "answer-8deef2d1-1973-51e5-9cbf-ea501d5e8c27" "answer-47fbec0e-7c87-50b2-b20a-31977a9c56d7" "answer-2ea5a4d8-cee6-5f5b-9559-0597059ae4e9" "answer-8370b066-0576-542b-8883-25e20f54d4ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-624998d8-03eb-57ee-930b-8fdefbbf7c6a" :answer/id #uuid "624998d8-03eb-57ee-930b-8fdefbbf7c6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3-{x}^{2}+4x}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8deef2d1-1973-51e5-9cbf-ea501d5e8c27" :answer/id #uuid "8deef2d1-1973-51e5-9cbf-ea501d5e8c27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+12x-9}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47fbec0e-7c87-50b2-b20a-31977a9c56d7" :answer/id #uuid "47fbec0e-7c87-50b2-b20a-31977a9c56d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+3}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ea5a4d8-cee6-5f5b-9559-0597059ae4e9" :answer/id #uuid "2ea5a4d8-cee6-5f5b-9559-0597059ae4e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8370b066-0576-542b-8883-25e20f54d4ec" :answer/id #uuid "8370b066-0576-542b-8883-25e20f54d4ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cbafb4bb-6bd6-540c-9367-06ab0b677b70" :question/id #uuid "cbafb4bb-6bd6-540c-9367-06ab0b677b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-126178" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{96}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}-3), & 1\\le x\\le 3 \\\\ 1, & x>3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{96}({2}^{4}+2(2)^{2}-3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{21}{96} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e8a9fa39-360a-5d80-8fca-fb43fa89be61"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e8a9fa39-360a-5d80-8fca-fb43fa89be61" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8a9fa39-360a-5d80-8fca-fb43fa89be61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" "answer-529bbff1-ee9c-5239-b9f3-b7e4f26f33fe" "answer-17a75073-455d-5976-ba1c-b3f22347a040" "answer-08f9e3f9-5178-5f25-af6a-daa6ab351cf7" "answer-3111cc62-9d7f-5a21-8f89-33bb0b009b9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" :answer/id #uuid "0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-529bbff1-ee9c-5239-b9f3-b7e4f26f33fe" :answer/id #uuid "529bbff1-ee9c-5239-b9f3-b7e4f26f33fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17a75073-455d-5976-ba1c-b3f22347a040" :answer/id #uuid "17a75073-455d-5976-ba1c-b3f22347a040" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08f9e3f9-5178-5f25-af6a-daa6ab351cf7" :answer/id #uuid "08f9e3f9-5178-5f25-af6a-daa6ab351cf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3111cc62-9d7f-5a21-8f89-33bb0b009b9c" :answer/id #uuid "3111cc62-9d7f-5a21-8f89-33bb0b009b9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{48}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a285feed-066b-52a2-a5c2-8c1c741cc3d0" :question/id #uuid "a285feed-066b-52a2-a5c2-8c1c741cc3d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-89738" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" :question/worked-solution "We can perform this computation using the complement, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-(1-{e}^{-4}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-29e83422-0d19-5c35-89b8-d714903a72c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-29e83422-0d19-5c35-89b8-d714903a72c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "29e83422-0d19-5c35-89b8-d714903a72c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6f86bba4-cf32-5b63-95b2-322fa3b1a857" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99eb6595-a15f-5755-a0e3-76f958a96458" "answer-4e656111-b56c-58e0-b523-b0edd9650549" "answer-6f86bba4-cf32-5b63-95b2-322fa3b1a857" "answer-616c4e05-5002-58ab-b3bb-58e10d3a8092" "answer-7b06527d-a247-549f-874c-21500db45064"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99eb6595-a15f-5755-a0e3-76f958a96458" :answer/id #uuid "99eb6595-a15f-5755-a0e3-76f958a96458" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e656111-b56c-58e0-b523-b0edd9650549" :answer/id #uuid "4e656111-b56c-58e0-b523-b0edd9650549" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f86bba4-cf32-5b63-95b2-322fa3b1a857" :answer/id #uuid "6f86bba4-cf32-5b63-95b2-322fa3b1a857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-616c4e05-5002-58ab-b3bb-58e10d3a8092" :answer/id #uuid "616c4e05-5002-58ab-b3bb-58e10d3a8092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b06527d-a247-549f-874c-21500db45064" :answer/id #uuid "7b06527d-a247-549f-874c-21500db45064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
